@startuml Incremental_Migration
title Incremental migration and protection points

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F8F8F8
  BorderColor #555555
}

start
:Architecture decision and corrected fixture contract;
note right
  Completed by this assessment.
  No standalone architecture-only code stage is required.
end note

:Stage 1 — shared XISF structural foundation;
note right
  Extract 16-byte envelope/range/event primitives.
  Correct prefix and strict UTF-8 behavior.
  First correctness fix lands in this stage.
  Unit/regression tests + range Kani candidate.
end note

fork
  :Stage 2A — migrate narrow pixel loader;
  note right
    Byte order, exact sample length,
    resolved attachment descriptors.
  end note
fork again
  :Stage 2B — migrate metadata extraction;
  note right
    Minimal raw-record boundary,
    FITSKeyword event parsing,
    preserve public semantic APIs.
  end note
fork again
  :Stage 2C — make validator consume shared structure;
  note right
    Validation policy remains separate;
    retain budgets and diagnostics.
  end note
end fork

:Remove old 12-byte/string-scanner paths
after parity tests pass;

:Stage 3 — Revision 1 codec and extension behavior;
note right
  Exact Zstandard frames, bounded zstd/zstd+sh loading,
  root extension handling, cancellation/resource tests,
  frame-window and subblock Kani candidates.
end note

:Stage 4 — coordinated release and AstroMuninn migration;
note right
  Publish shared crates, update consumer versions,
  run validation/metadata/path-plan golden tests.
end note

:Stage 5 — post-Revision-1 hardening;
note right
  Raw Property preservation, schema invariants,
  detached-signature compatibility, storage corpus.
  Selective FITS cleanup may begin here.
end note

if (Evidence justifies FITS/API cleanup?) then (yes)
  :Cards-based FITS metadata input,
  private proofable arithmetic extraction,
  remove unused metrics dependencies;
else (no)
  :Keep mature CFITSIO paths and public APIs unchanged;
endif

:Deferred: generic format AST,
generic image framework, pure-Rust FITS replacement;
stop
@enduml
